NEARS-3441 QA — AC2 raw HTTP replay evidence (order 172, store 35 "Test Store",
coupon NEARS10 expired 2026-09-06, today 2026-09-11)

Real vendor session (ts@ts.com, logged in via the real /login/vendor form),
same CSRF token/cookies the live #edit-order-amount modal form would submit.
POST /vendor-panel/order/update-order-amount  order_id=172  order_amount=39

Response:
HTTP/1.1 407 Proxy Authentication Required   <- literal reason phrase for
                                                 HTTP status 407; body is
                                                 the app's own JSON, not a
                                                 real proxy challenge
Content-Type: application/json
X-Request-Id: a3cc0228-be22-4c4d-b06d-1aa974b933a1

Body: {"errors":[{"code":"coupon","message":"Coupon expire"}]}

DB check after: orders.id=172 order_amount UNCHANGED at 39.00 (no partial
write on the error path).

NOTE (regression-candidate, pre-existing, unrelated to this ticket's diff):
driving this same POST from an actual Chrome browser (Playwright, real
#edit-order-amount modal, real form submit) fails client-side with
net::ERR_UNEXPECTED_PROXY_AUTH and lands on chrome-error://chromewebdata/ --
Chromium's network stack special-cases ANY literal HTTP 407 response (even
from the origin server, not an actual configured proxy) as a proxy-auth
challenge and never delivers it to the page. This is pre-existing: the
literal `407` HTTP status is returned by CouponLogic::is_valide()'s expired-
coupon branch and mapped straight to response()->json([...], 407) at
multiple call sites across the codebase (not introduced or touched by
NEARS-3441's diff, which only changed the module_id argument). Confirmed via
raw curl replay above (same session, same CSRF token) that the SERVER
response is correct (407 JSON, not 500) -- the defect is purely in how a
real Chrome browser mishandles that literal status code client-side.
